# Hopper's NetBird patches, in apply order (later ones build on earlier ones).
# Second word on: phone = the app's library (netbird/build-phone.sh), exit = the exit servers' client
# (netbird/build-client.sh, copied to the public repo by publish-client.sh).
# A line with "wireguard" applies to the wireguard-go checkout instead of NetBird.

# With NB_GRPC_WEBSOCKET=true, gRPC to a self-hosted server rides its WebSocket wrapper, for hosts behind a proxy that does not pass gRPC.
netbird-grpc-websocket.patch phone exit
# Each peer update switches on Maybenot padding when NB_DAITA_MACHINES holds machines, and full-size packets when NB_DAITA_FULL_SIZE=true.
netbird-daita.patch phone exit
# Connections to the host in NB_ECH_HOST use ECH after a DNS-over-HTTPS lookup, or are refused; QUIC to it is skipped.
netbird-ech.patch phone exit
# The answer goes out before ICE candidates, so a direct link can form in the first round instead of after minutes on the relay. Drop both this and hold-candidates once netbirdio/netbird#8443 is fixed upstream.
netbird-answer-first.patch phone exit
# Each new ICE agent gets the remote candidates of the last 5 s.
netbird-hold-candidates.patch phone exit
# Caps gRPC's reconnect wait for Management and Signal at 30 s, down from 120 s, so a client reaches a server soon after it wakes.
netbird-grpc-reconnect-cap.patch phone exit
# Mullvad's DAITA ported to the batched send path, with the Maybenot BlockOutgoing action; built with Rust maybenot-ffi for arm64.
wireguard-daita.patch wireguard phone exit
